{"url": "https://www.sdstate.edu/programs/graduate/biological-sciences-phd", "final_url": "https://www.sdstate.edu/programs/graduate/biological-sciences-phd", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-28", "text": "Biological Sciences (Ph.D.) | Academic Program | South Dakota State University\nSkip to main content\nApply\nVisit\nDirectories\nDegree Finder\nFaculty and Staff\nOffice Directory\nBuildings Directory\nEvent Calendar\nCampus Map\nSDSTATE\nSearch\nVisit\nDegree Finder\nCampus Map\nSDSTATE\nSearch\nFilter by Topic\nBlog Event News Profile Program\nClose Search Box\nMain Navigation\nAbout\nAbout Us\nUniversity Facts\nNews\nSandbox Login\nAwards and Rankings\nConsumer Information\nAccreditation\nAcademics\nColleges and Departments/Schools\nGeneral Education\nAcademic Calendar\nAcademic Catalog\nGraduate School\nHonors College\nLibrary\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate\nTransfer\nGraduate\nInternational\nOnline\nDual Credit\nPaying for College\nStudent Life\nHousing\nCampus Dining\nStudent Success\nStudent Experience\nUniversity Wellbeing\nParents and Families\nResearch\nEvents and Trainings\nFind Funding\nResearch Impact\nProposal Development\nResearch Support\nStudent Research Opportunities\nCommunity\nAttractions\nCamps and Conferences\nFamily Weekend\nSDState Experience\nSDSU Metro Center\nEvent Calendar\nSearch\nApply Today\nSDSTATE\nBreadcrumb\n...\nHome\nAcademics\nDegree Finder\nBiological Sciences (Ph.D.)\nBiological Sciences (Ph.D.)\nPh.D.\nBrookings Main Campus\nShare\nTwitter\nLinkedin\nFacebook\nEmail\nPrint\nApply Now\nMore Information\nPreparing scientists to solve grand challenges.\nAre you interested in preparing for a career that positions you to address critical issues such as efficient food production, natural resource sustainability, quality of life and health of humans, animals and plants? If so, a Ph.D. in biological sciences just might be for you.\nThis is a cooperative program leading to the Doctor of Philosophy degree in biological sciences. Departments that cooperate in the program are:\nAgricultural and biosystems engineering\nAgronomy, horticulture and plant science\nAnimal science\nBiology and microbiology\nDairy and food science\nHealth and nutritional sciences\nNatural resource management\nVeterinary and biomedical sciences\nThe doctoral programs in biological sciences allow for considerable latitude in the education and training of students. The plan of study can be designed to meet the interests and individual needs of the student. While the training of most students is largely directed to a single discipline represented within one of the participating departments, cross-disciplinary training is available.\nVisit Department\nView Requirements\nCost and Aid\nQuick Facts\nLocations\nBrookings Main Campus\nCredits\n60 Credit Plan\n90 Credit Plan\nEst. Time to Completion\n3-5 years\nStart Term\nFall, Spring, Summer\nIs it for you?\nThis program will be a good fit if you:\nHave an undergraduate or master\u2019s degree in basic science, agriculture, food science, nutrition or natural resources.\nWant to develop multidisciplinary expertise to address complex problems.\nEnjoy life and natural sciences and want to address critical issues related to efficient food production, natural resource management, environmental sustainability or health of plants, animal or humans.\nJob Outlook\nBack to top\nCareer Opportunities\nExplore possible career opportunities with this degree:\nDesign and manage efficient food production systems\nNatural resource management and conservation\nLaboratory research\nProduct development\nQuality control and food safety\nHuman, animal and plant health\nReady to take the next step?\nContact Our Department\nYajun Wu\nVisit Department\n605-688-5974\nHelpful Resources\nProgram Requirements\nDomestic Applicants\nInternational Applicants\nTuition and Funding\nGraduate Assistantships\nApply Now\nGraduate Admissions\nGraduate School\nYou may also be interested in...\nPharmaceu